  "version": 196,
  "released": "2026-08-23",
  "changelog": "v196: whispers and keystone questions. NOMENCLATURE (owner-set): a WHISPER is information woven into a conversation that fits naturally, drawn from a developed arc, serving a second agenda beyond the conversation's own — general by design, with three rules every kind inherits (only where it fits, at most one per conversation, never penalized); the TIMELINE WHISPER is the first kind — the timeline finally gets ASKED, and the deferral side-state is deleted. WHISPERS: the week's arc card carries a keystone's REAL probe, its identity (tl:<anchor-slug>), the person's own anchors, its leverage and the unknowns one answer would place (arc_planner._timeline_gap_intent, ranked by leverage with era-affinity as the tiebreak; timeline_interaction.whisper_from_keystone). conversation._assemble_session_block and {arc_card_current_intent} render the probe and the landmarks for a timeline item and are byte-identical for every other intent kind (golden); turn-instructions.md carries the direction — raise it only where it fits, at most one per conversation, accept any precision (a range places things), never press, never open with a year. New sixth lint class timeline_gates.one_per_conversation (caller-counted, like no_new_bound_streak) plus the lane's first three goldens: the whisper that fits and files, the one that never fits, the partial range. KEYSTONE QUESTIONS: a keystone whose leverage clears the ONE dial timeline_leverage_per_story (6 — an exchange rate: how many unknowns one answer must place to be worth one ordinary story answer) is MINTED as an ordinary bank row in the new `timeline` group (mint_keystone_question / insert_keystone_question / timeline_probe_index, all pure; GROUP_CAPS['timeline'] holds it to one a week; asked once, answered once, never re-asked by the bank's own mechanism). v195's leverage_boost adjacency nudge, keystone_slugs and current_keystone_slugs are DELETED — lifting a question because its focus resembled a keystone is what starred a question that never asks for a date (lifehug/lifehug-platform#586). REPLY ROUTING: run_post_answer_turn derives the turn's timeline item from ONE definition (timeline_item_for_session over the arc card and the minted-probe index), sets TurnShape.timeline_stage — the only thing that puts `placed` in the output contract — stores the validated record on the turn, stamps timeline_probe_id, and files it through `lifehug.py timeline-place`; the next compile re-derives. A RANGE WITH A BASIS is first-class. DELETED: state/timeline_deferred.json, DEFERRED_FILE, DEFERRED_QUIET_DAYS, defer_unknown, is_deferred, load_deferred, the `deferred` fields, the vault-contract entry and every doc mention — \"I'll find out\" is an ordinary answer that files nothing (remnant guard test). ARC LEARNING: the weekly judgment-update step gains an arc-yield pass over data the vault already has (session documents: filed answers, placements, new entities per arc-card intent kind) and may make one bounded, evidence-cited amendment to state/question_judgment/arc_learned.md, composed into the arc-plan prompt as `## Arc judgment signals` — same ADR 0009 mechanism (cursor / no-op / compaction), never an edit to the framework template. Passive users are untouched: with no keystone clearing the cutoff the queue and the daily send are byte-identical to v195. UNKNOWNS ARE CONCRETE (owner-set on staging the same day — the /timeline page offered \"UNPLACED EVENTS — 116 moment(s) I can't place in any period\" with the probe \"Tell me what happened\"): unknowns() never emits an aggregate row again — every unknown is ONE subject with a human label (a titled moment, an era's missing bounds, a place's span, a dated hole between two named bands, a contradiction), the six aggregate kinds become counts on the new unknown_ledger, dependency_index indexes the concrete keys on both sides, offered_unknowns caps a page at UNKNOWNS_PAGE_CAP (30) by leverage, every PROBE_TEXTS rung names {label}, KIND_OPENERS gives each kind its own opening question (bare and anchored), the bare \"tell me what happened\" probe survives only for a single moment with no anchors, and keystone_probe() gives every starred anchor a real question about itself. A golden per unknown kind and per keystone anchor kind, bare and anchored. Contract: docs/pr-specs/timeline-whispers-and-keystones.md. Decision: ADR 0024 (amended 2026-08-23).",
